## 📖 About

**Tropsi X** is a non-GKI kernel for the OnePlus 8, 8 Pro, and 8T, built on top of
[**ppajda's XTD kernel**](https://github.com/ppajda) with manually integrated
**KernelSU-Next** hooks, a modern LLVM toolchain, and a systemless AnyKernel3 installer.
It's built for daily-driver stability first, with performance and root access layered
on top without breaking OTA compatibility.

> ⚠️ **Disclaimer:** Flashing a custom kernel carries risk of instability, bootloops,
> or other issues. You flash entirely at your own risk — the maintainer is not
> responsible for any damage to your device.

---

## ✨ Features

- 🧠 **KernelSU-Next** — manually integrated hooks for root management without a modified boot image
- 🛠️ **Neutron Clang 19.0.0 + Neutron LLD** — full LLVM toolchain build (no GCC)
- 📦 **Systemless AnyKernel3 installer** — OTA-friendly, compatible with autoflash apps
- 🐧 **Linux 4.19.325-cip132** base, rebased on `blu_spark`
- 🔋 Tuned for a balance of battery life and performance out of the box

---

## 📱 Supported Devices

| Device | Codename | Variants |
|---|---|---|
| OnePlus 8 | `instantnoodle` | Global, T-Mobile, Verizon, Visible |
| OnePlus 8 Pro | `instantnoodlep` | Global |
| OnePlus 8T | `kebab` / `kebabt` | Global |

---

## 📥 Installation

1. Make sure your bootloader is **unlocked** and you're on a compatible ROM/firmware base.
2. Download the latest flashable zip from the [XDA thread](https://xdaforums.com/t/kernel-4-19-op8-pro-t-tropsi_x-vx-x-custom-kernelsu.4794907/) or the repo's Releases page.
3. Flash the zip via **TWRP**, a custom recovery, or a fastboot-based autoflash app — over your current stock/custom boot setup.
4. Reboot. First boot after flashing may take a little longer than usual.

---

## 🏗️ Building From Source

```bash
# Clone the source
git clone -b sm8250_t_13.1_op8 https://github.com/TropsPk/Tropsi_X_Kernel.git
cd Tropsi_X_Kernel

# Grab the Neutron Clang toolchain, then point your environment at it
export PATH="$(pwd)/../neutron-clang/bin:$PATH"

# Build (adjust config target for your device)
make O=out ARCH=arm64 <device_defconfig>
make O=out ARCH=arm64 -j$(nproc --all)
